<article class="env-lemma" id="00F9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00F9">Lemma <span data-tag="00F9">10.29.5</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $f$ be an element of $R$. Let $S = R_ f$. Then the image of a constructible subset of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S)$ is constructible in $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We repeatedly use Lemma <a href="/tag/00F6" data-tag="00F6">10.29.1</a> without mention. Let $U, V$ be quasi-compact open in $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S)$. We will show that the image of $U \cap V^ c$ is constructible. Under the identification $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S) = D(f)$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/00E4" data-tag="00E4">10.17.6</a> the sets $U, V$ correspond to quasi-compact opens $U', V'$ of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$. Hence it suffices to show that $U' \cap (V')^ c$ is constructible in $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ which is clear. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>